      "content": "wait, an electromagnetic pulse? that sounds way more serious than just a bad bulb. do you think it's possible the pulse is actually a way for the devices to send data out? like, if the phone call triggers a signal that the bulbs then pick up and transmit back to the hub or something... i've noticed the flickering happens even when my phone is on silent.",
